 "description": "Version 6.0 of the Crimson Hexagon Fractal Navigation Map, a non-lossy interface for traversing the archive’s rooms, institutions, heteronyms, operators, integrity structures, and hidden routes. Rather than summarize the architecture, it encodes a probabilistic field of gravity and affordance: queries are directed toward deeper documents through container types and decompression protocols while retaining at least one depth gate.\n\nThe map describes the January 2026 architecture as 201 DOI-anchored documents organized across narrative, systems, and interface layers. It supersedes v5.3 without invalidating that historical layer and distinguishes rooms, chambers, vaults, porticos, portals, and commissions by the kind of traversal each permits.",
